# Keep the build context to sources + ops scripts. Notably excluded:
# - runtimes/: host-fetched macOS dylibs; the Dockerfile fetches the Linux
#   .so for the image platform itself, and the Directory.Build.props glob
#   would otherwise copy stale mac binaries into the Linux publish.
# - data/, logs/, mail/, mark-read/, secrets/, mbsyncrc*, .env*, compose
#   overrides: deploy-host state that lives in the compose dir (= this repo clone on the VM). The
#   build stage does `COPY . .`, so without these exclusions every on-host
#   build shipped the entire Maildir into the build context and copied the
#   Fastmail password file into build-stage layers. Never let bind-mount
#   state or secrets near the image.
.git
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
build/
coverage/
data/
dist/
logs/
mail/
mark-read/
mbsyncrc
mbsyncrc.*
compose.override.yml
compose.override.yaml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml
# Review write-ups of a live install (gitignored, kept on disk at the root).
*REVIEW*.md
runtimes/
secrets/
# The static product site (published by .github/workflows/pages.yml) is
# never part of the image; excluding it also keeps a site-only edit from
# invalidating the `COPY . .` layer and rebuilding every .NET project.
site/
.env
.env.*
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/appsettings.Local.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite.bak.*
